  "spaced.tut.s1.text": {"en":"The Spaced switch gives you a smart schedule. Each word comes back just before you would forget it, so you spend time where it helps most. Flip it on or off any time.","haw":""},
  "spaced.tut.s1.title": {"en":"Turn it on","haw":""},
  "spaced.tut.s2.text": {"en":"Your deck is the words that are due, plus a few new ones (5 in a small set, 10 in a bigger one). Words that are not due yet stay hidden until their time.","haw":""},
  "spaced.tut.s2.title": {"en":"Due and new cards","haw":""},
  "spaced.tut.s3.text": {"en":"Correct pushes a word further away. Incorrect brings it back soon. In Writing, a right answer on the first try counts as correct; hints and give-ups bring it back sooner.","haw":""},
  "spaced.tut.s3.title": {"en":"Correct and Incorrect","haw":""},
  "spaced.tut.s4.text": {"en":"New and missed words start with short steps: 10 minutes, then 60 minutes. After that the gaps grow: 1 day, 6 days, and longer each time you get it right.","haw":""},
  "spaced.tut.s4.title": {"en":"Short steps, then days","haw":""},
  "spaced.tut.s5.text": {"en":"A badge above the card says what is happening. \"Review missed\" and \"Study full set anyway\" are practice only: they never change your schedule.","haw":""},
  "spaced.tut.s5.title": {"en":"Counts or practice","haw":""},
  "spaced.tut.s6.text": {"en":"Schedules are kept per word and per mode, so Flashcards and Writing are separate. They save to your account when you are signed in, or to this browser if not. Your answers are saved when you finish the deck; leave early and nothing is saved. The page checks what is due only when it builds a deck, so reload or reopen the set to refresh.","haw":""},
  "spaced.tut.s6.title": {"en":"Saved for you","haw":""},
